    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYANS0K39CS6BWN3SMH\"><strong>Overview</strong></h2>\n<p>The activity logger is a self-service audit trail that provides visibility into all actions performed within your Klaviyo account. Instead of contacting Klaviyo support to investigate account changes, you can now independently track who made a change, what that change was, and when it happened.</p>\n<p>This transparency helps ensure account security, simplifies compliance auditing, and allows you to quickly troubleshoot configuration issues by identifying the source of specific updates.</p>\n<p>In this article, you will learn:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Who can access the activity logger.</li>\n<li>The benefits of using the audit trail for your business.</li>\n<li>How to navigate and filter the log.</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYFZ51TA10VDQT70JSZ\"><strong>Access and permissions</strong></h2>\n<p>To ensure account security, the activity logger is not visible to all users. It is available exclusively to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Account Owners</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Admins</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Users with \"Account Settings\" permissions</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYG0CBA04A8W69XKQ8S\"><strong>Benefits of the activity logger</strong></h2>\n<p>Using the activity logger allows you to manage your account more effectively without the need for external assistance.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Enhanced Visibility:</strong> Gain a clear view of user behavior across your entire organization to see \"who is doing what\" in real-time.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Streamlined Troubleshooting:</strong> Quickly resolve support or configuration issues by identifying exactly when a setting or campaign was modified.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Security and Compliance:</strong> Maintain a permanent record of all account edits to meet internal or external security audit requirements.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Self-Service Efficiency:</strong> Eliminate the need to email Klaviyo Support to verify historical account actions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYJNGJS5G99FY92XW8F\"><strong>How to use the activity logger</strong></h2>\n<p>To access the logger, navigate to <strong>Settings &gt; Account &gt; Activity Logger</strong>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYJ3M9VBHANG7NBSWRC\"><strong>View edit actions</strong></h3>\n<p>The log provides a comprehensive list of all <strong>edit actions</strong> performed in your account. Each entry includes the timestamp, the user's email address, and the category of the change.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYKVTN5MZWASEPJDBS7\"><strong>Filter and search</strong></h3>\n<p>Use the search and filter tools to narrow down the log by:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>User:</strong> Track the activity of a specific team member.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Timeframe:</strong> Audit changes made during a specific launch or reporting period.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Keyword:</strong> Search for specific flow titles, segment names, or campaign IDs.</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYMH525N5R0QRAK09CG\"><strong>Open beta limitations</strong></h2>\n<p>This feature is currently in <strong>open beta</strong>. While the log captures 100% of edit actions, the \"Event Details\" (the specific granular data about what was changed within an item) are currently limited.</p>\n<p>We are adding these granular details incrementally as we move toward General Availability (GA).</p>\n<p>[!TIP] <strong>Need more information?</strong> If you see an action in the logger but require more specific details that are not yet available in the beta interface, please reach out to<a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/requests/new\">Klaviyo Support</a> for additional assistance.</p>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KCSV8PYPRATF5NBWX70ZN0PH\"><strong>Additional resources</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005251468\">How to manage users and permissions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005073107\">How to update your account settings</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>",
